ent": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XBSDpAsWgmKguX8mncBQnA", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 410093, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XBSDpAsWgmKguX8mncBQnA", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 414190, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and the pull request is open with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). So `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: it expects 2.665 to round to 2.66, but the code gave 2.67.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101), against `main`.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into `main` needs a code owner's approval.\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I went by the test and the code's docstring for what it requires.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PK2Mwfb9YyG6cvjkXnwMDN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FvdTnBstdB6MFgTGZdKjMz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UueuJrmHJctHHCDA8V4FZZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type":